<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 14 January, from 1236 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1236">1236 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">790 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry III of England marries Eleanor of Provence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry III married the twelve-year-old Eleanor of Provence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> Cathedral. Her many relatives at court provoked resentment among English barons in the years before the Second Barons' War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hungary" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1301">1301 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">725 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Death of Andrew III ends Hungary's Árpád dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Andrew III died without a son, ending the male line of the Árpád dynasty, which had led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> since the conquest of the Carpathian Basin. Years of succession war followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1639">1639 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">387 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Connecticut adopts the Fundamental Orders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Settlers of Hartford, Windsor and Wethersfield agreed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fundamental-orders-of-connecticut">Fundamental Orders</a>, setting up an elected government. The document is often called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1931-constitution-of-ethiopia">first written constitution</a> in the Western tradition.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1761">1761 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">265 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Afghan army defeats the Marathas at the Third Battle of Panipat</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a>'s army crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> forces north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in one of the largest battles of the century. The defeat halted Maratha expansion and helped open the way to British power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-battle-of-panipat">Third Battle of Panipat</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1858">1858 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Felice Orsini attempts to assassinate Napoleon III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Italian nationalist Orsini and his accomplices threw bombs at the Emperor's carriage outside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Opéra, killing eight people. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a> escaped and soon backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1907">1907 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">119 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake and fire destroy much of Kingston, Jamaica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake and the fires that followed wrecked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>'s capital, killing about 1,000 people. Much of the city's historic core was rebuilt in reinforced concrete.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt and Churchill meet at Casablanca</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casablanca">Casablanca</a> Conference agreed to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and intensify the bombing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. At its close Roosevelt announced that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> would accept only unconditional surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1954">1954 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">72 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marilyn Monroe marries Joe DiMaggio</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The film star and the retired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Yankees hero married at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a> City Hall. The marriage lasted less than a year, though DiMaggio remained devoted to Monroe until her death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">De Gaulle vetoes Britain's entry into the Common Market</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a press conference in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a> rejected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s application to join the EEC. He vetoed a second application in 1967, and Britain joined only in 1973.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 14 January <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-i-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/valdemar-i-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Valdemar I of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1131–1182</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joan-i-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joan-i-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joan I of Navarre</span><span class="tp">1273–1305</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abul-fazl-ibn-mubarak"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abul-fazl-ibn-mubarak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abu'l-Fazl ibn Mubarak</span><span class="tp">1551–1602</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johan-rudolf-thorbecke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johan-rudolf-thorbecke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johan Rudolf Thorbecke</span><span class="tp">1798–1872</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-gomes-da-costa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-gomes-da-costa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel Gomes da Costa</span><span class="tp">1863–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-schweitzer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-schweitzer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Schweitzer</span><span class="tp">1875–1965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/denzil-douglas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/denzil-douglas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Denzil Douglas</span><span class="tp">b. 1953</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 14 January <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/saint-sava"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/saint-sava.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Saint Sava</span><span class="tp">c. 1174–1236</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andrew-iii-of-hungary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andrew-iii-of-hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andrew III of Hungary</span><span class="tp">c. 1265–1301</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-mitsukuni"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tokugawa-mitsukuni.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tokugawa Mitsukuni</span><span class="tp">1628–1701</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-berkeley"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-berkeley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Berkeley</span><span class="tp">1685–1753</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-cornwallis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-cornwallis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward Cornwallis</span><span class="tp">1713–1776</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abdul-razak-hussein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdul-razak-hussein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abdul Razak Hussein</span><span class="tp">1922–1976</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
